course: dictionary
lesson: 1636
title: The many meanings of child
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A child is usually a young boy or girl. But the word can also mean someone's son or daughter, at any age. «Grandma has three children.» Her children may be grown up with families of their own, and they are still her children. Children means more than one child.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is in use. «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them, and they are just as much part of it.» Here child means a son or daughter, because adopted children become a true part of the family.
explain: Word choice changes the feeling. Kid and kiddo are casual, friendly words for a child. «Don't be such a child» is a rough put-down, meaning you are being silly or babyish. Official notices use words like minor or pupil instead.
fact: A child is a young boy or girl.
fact: Someone's son or daughter is also their child, at any age: «Grandma has three children.»
fact: Children is the plural of child, meaning more than one child.
fact: «Kid» and «kiddo» are casual, friendly words for a child.
fact: «Don't be such a child» is a put-down meaning you are being silly or babyish.
exercise: «Some children are adopted: they join a family that did not give birth to them.» In this sentence, what does child mean? | A school subject | A young animal | A kind of game | *A son or daughter in a family
exercise: Mia says, «Don't be such a child!» to her brother. What does she mean? | He has lost his bag | He is very kind and helpful | *He is being silly or babyish | He is the oldest in the family
exercise: Which word is the plural of child? | childs | *children | childen | childrens
test: Which word is a casual, friendly word for a child? | minor | juvenile | *kiddo | dependant
test: In «Grandma has three children», what does children mean? | Pupils at a school | Young animals | Toys | *Grandma's sons and daughters
exam: In a formal notice, which word means the same as child? | rug rat | kiddo | nipper | *minor
